# DFThub environment file (optional)
#
# Local use does not need this file. `dfthub serve` listens on
# 127.0.0.1:8188, keeps its data under ~/.local/share/dfthub (or
# $XDG_DATA_HOME/dfthub) and sends no e-mail; `dfthub serve --local` also
# skips registration and sign-in on a computer only you use.
#
# For a server: copy this file outside the installation and the Git checkout,
# make it private and name it in DFTHUB_ENV_FILE before starting:
#   chmod 600 /etc/dfthub/dfthub.env
#   DFTHUB_ENV_FILE=/etc/dfthub/dfthub.env dfthub serve
#
# Format: one KEY=value per line; lines starting with # are ignored. Do not put
# a comment after a value on the same line. An empty value (KEY=) counts as
# unset. Variables already set in the process environment take precedence,
# and the --data-dir and --python options take precedence over both.
# On/off settings accept 1/0 (also true/false, yes/no, on/off).

# --- Service -----------------------------------------------------------------
DFTHUB_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/dfthub/data
# Public address of the site; used for links in e-mails.
# DFTHUB_PUBLIC_URL=https://dfthub.example.org
# Enable only after HTTPS works at the reverse proxy.
# DFTHUB_ENABLE_HSTS=1
# Signing key for login tokens. By default a random key is created once in
# <data dir>/.jwt_secret; set this only to share a key between installations.
# JWT_SECRET=

# --- Compute environment (defaults: current Python, packaged optimizer) ------
# DFTHUB_PYTHON=/opt/dfthub/.venv/bin/python
# DFTHUB_TMB11_DIR=/path/to/custom-optimizer
# DFTHUB_DEMO_ROOT=/var/lib/dfthub/optimizer
# DFTHUB_AME418_ROOT=/path/to/external-AME418-checkpoints

# --- Resources (defaults detect CPU/RAM and Linux container limits) ----------
# DFTHUB_CPU_THREADS=16
# DFTHUB_TASK_THREADS=8
# DFTHUB_MEMORY_MB=16000
# DFTHUB_DFT_TASKS=2
# DFTHUB_OPTIMIZER_THREADS=4

# --- E-mail notifications (off by default) -----------------------------------
# When on, DFThub e-mails the job owner when a job is submitted and when it
# completes or fails. To turn it on, uncomment the whole block, including
# DFTHUB_MAIL_SUPPRESS=0, and also set DFTHUB_PUBLIC_URL above.
# `dfthub serve` prints "Mail: on ..." or "Mail: off ..." at startup.
# Use either USE_TLS (STARTTLS, usually port 587) or USE_SSL (usually port 465).
# DFTHUB_MAIL_SUPPRESS=0
# DFTHUB_MAIL_SERVER=smtp.example.org
# DFTHUB_MAIL_PORT=587
# DFTHUB_MAIL_USE_TLS=1
# DFTHUB_MAIL_USE_SSL=0
# DFTHUB_MAIL_USERNAME=your-account
# DFTHUB_MAIL_PASSWORD=replace-me
# DFTHUB_MAIL_SENDER=DFThub <noreply@example.org>
